title: bellemere_Gift_Hunt_Stationary
location: town
---

You walk into the little well-lit shop and find the pleasant scent of fresh paper and hints of floral perfume waft through the air. The room is small and tightly packed, the isles narrow and every shelf lined with precisely organized rows of inks jars and homemade paper and fancy fountain pens. For such a tiny shop, you find there is just so much to look at.
{$name}: Excuse me?
The shopkeeper is a middle aged woman with a pleasant smile, and she turns to help you right away.
Shopkeeper: Yes? What are you looking for?
{$name}: I’m not sure… I need a gift for a friend. She, uh…
Shopkeeper: Oh? Is she someone special then? Hmm? A special someone?
You feel your face go red, despite your best attempts not to react, and stumble through your next sentence.
{$name}: Uh, she, uh, maybe…
Shopkeeper: And what does she like? Flowers? Cute animals? 
She holds up a picture of the strangests little lion-flower hybrid on a card, and for the briefest moment you consider buying it… it does seem just odd enough that Bellemere might like it, but you shake your head. You can’t take chances on something this important!
And then you spot it: scented stationary kits.
{$name}: Ah! Do you have one of those kits in a mikan scent, maybe?
Shopkeeper: We do have a citrus scent, yes!
Is this the perfect New Year’s gift?
-> Yes
	<<jump bellemere_Gift_Hunt_PaperYes>>
-> No, better keep shopping
	<<jump bellemere_Gift_Hunt_choices>>
===

title: bellemere_Gift_Hunt_PaperYes
location: town
---

You know Bellemere misses her kids, even if she’s intimated that one of those kids is rather hard to get ahold of (being, er, an outlaw). Maybe she would like the idea of writing to them with paper that reminded them of home? Maybe such a gift would make her feel closer to those she loved, and therefore close to home, herself?
You smile a little, knowing she’d appreciate the thought.
===

title: bellemere_Gift_Hunt_Fruit
location: town
---

Passing down the street casually, a colorful stand loaded with piles of fruit catches your eye. A lot of it you’ve never seen before in your life– imported delicacies of every shape and color and size you could imagine are in crates stacked one on top of another and in tilted bins meant to entice the eye.
A gift for Bellemere? Well, what makes more sense than her favorite fruit?
Of course they have mikans here; it’s even the exact same variety you’ve seen her growing, straight from her home island.
Is this the perfect New Year’s gift?
-> Yes
	<<jump bellemere_Gift_Hunt_FruitYes>>
-> No, better keep shopping
	<<jump bellemere_Gift_Hunt_choices>>
===

title: bellemere_Gift_Hunt_FruitYes
location: town
---

{$name}: I’ll take a dozen. And, uh… do you wrap them? Like, in a fancy basket?
The young woman running the stand enthusiastically agrees, pulling out a wide roll of cellophane and getting to work, and before long you’re carrying an oversized basket of mikans wrapped lovingly with a big blue bow.
===

title: bellemere_Gift_Hunt_Jerky
location: town
---

The jerky stand is half-obscured by steaming grills, the little old man behind the  curtains of meats nearly rendered invisible. If not for the man’s shouting and the obnoxious waving red sale signs, it would be hard to even identify as a shop.
Bellemere is a tough lady. Somehow, you feel like she’d appreciate some of the rare meats for sale, here.
Maybe they would make a good gift?
And then you see it… and you have to laugh.
She told you about Arlong, the fishman pirate from her island. He was a sawshark fishman, right? 
And, hanging over the drying smoke on a rack, was a very blizzard cut of fish labeled clearly as “sawshark jerky.”
It was pricey, and didn’t look particularly tasty, but you figured you could buy an assortment of meats along with that one as a unique gift. It was funny! Funny gifts made good New Years gifts, right?
Is this the perfect New Year’s gift?
-> Yes
	<<jump bellemere_Gift_Hunt_JerkyYes>>
-> No, better keep shopping
	<<jump bellemere_Gift_Hunt_choices>>
===

title: bellemere_Gift_Hunt_JerkyYes
location: town
---

{$name}: I’ll take one of these, and an assortment of whatever other exotic jerky you have that you think a super-cool marine would like!
Shopkeeper: You got it!
He wraps your wares in newspaper and you cheerfully head off, excited for your moment at midnight.
===